WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.002
-Hello, everyone and welcome
back to the captain's quarters.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.470
If you watched last night's
"Closer Look,"

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.872
you may have noticed that
my parents were visiting,

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:09.942
and it was the first time
my father and the sea captain

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:12.078
were in the same room,
which was awkward,

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.280
as my dad is on the record

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.383
as not being a fan
of the captain.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:21.087
-To be fair, Larry also
doesn't like the Beatles.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.089
-That is a true fact
about my dad.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.523
He doesn't like the Beatles.

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:26.859
But we made time for my father
and the sea captain

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.194
to hash it out, and at the end
of tonight's episode

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:31.998
we're going to show you
that exclusive conversation.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:35.768
-Our discourse, like the sea,
got a bit rocky.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:38.437
-Speaking of rocky waters --
-Forced segue!

00:00:38.437 --> 00:00:40.239
-The President knows he
can't win in November

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.541
with a majority of votes,
so instead he's trying to

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:44.377
undermine the integrity
of the election

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.512
by sabotaging
the post office.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:48.781
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:52.585
♪♪

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.087
Throughout the entirety
of his term,

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.588
Donald Trump has
consistently been

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.423
the most unpopular President
in history.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:00.626
It's easy to forget, but he's
been widely disliked

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.562
since day one of his campaign.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.330
People might have thought
they liked the character

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.932
of Donald Trump
on "The Apprentice,"

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.434
but that's a little like
enjoying Buzz Lightyear

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.135
when you're watching
"Toy Story"

00:01:10.135 --> 00:01:11.871
and then meeting
the Buzz Lightyear

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.739
in Times Square.
[ Inhales ]

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:16.176
"To infinity and let's get
this picture over.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.177
I've got to take a dump, kid,
and it takes like 15 minutes

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:19.578
to get this suit off."

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:21.881
Trump has never once cracked
50% approval

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.382
in the Gallup
daily tracking poll,

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:24.684
which is unprecedented.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.520
Even the "Cats" movie has
a 53% audience score

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.622
on Rotten Tomatoes,
although I guess

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.157
unlike the "Cats" movie,

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.759
the White House can't just
digitally blur out the [bleep].

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:36.829
Trump and the Republican Party
have largely given up

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.698
on the idea of persuading
a majority of voters

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.234
to side with them,
the way you normally would

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.768
in a healthy democracy.

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:45.404
The modern conservative movement
is a fundamentally

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:48.741
anti-majoritarian movement
based on excluding people,

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.342
not including them.

00:01:50.342 --> 00:01:53.613
It's not a coincidence their
paragon owns private golf clubs.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.481
The Republican Party
motto should be,

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.350
"Sorry, you're not on
the list."

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.785
Their only hope of gaining
and holding on to power

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:01.354
is through tactics like
gerrymandering,

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:04.223
voter suppression, the electoral
college, stacking the courts,

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:05.925
or colluding with foreign
governments, which is why

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:08.560
Trump has spent the last
four years cold-calling

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.297
random countries asking them
to help him cheat.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.499
[ As Trump ] "Hello, Peru, do
you have any dirt on Joe Biden?

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.602
"Joe. Biden.
Loves trains.

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.237
Looks super cool on a bicycle."

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.073
Now, Trump got impeached
for that, of course.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.841
So he's moved on
to his next scheme,

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.643
sabotaging the post office.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.044
-New today,
the "Washington Post" reporting

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.480
a sweeping overhaul of
the U.S. Postal Service.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.249
It was announced in a memo
late Friday

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.484
from Postmaster General
Louis DeJoy.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:34.553
The "Post" writes, "The move
displaced two top executives

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:36.589
overseeing day-to-day
operations."

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.559
-This is coming as Democrats
are calling for an investigation

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:42.762
into DeJoy
and his operating measures

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.364
that some say have
slowed mail delivery service.

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:46.732
-That's right.
Late on Friday,

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:49.034
the Postal Service announced
a massive restructuring

00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:51.503
that centers power around
the postmaster general,

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:56.642
Louis DeJoy, a Trump loyalist
who donated over $360,000

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.745
to the Trump campaign and
Republican National Committee.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.780
And right off the bat
you know it's shady

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.948
because they did it
late on a Friday night.

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:05.351
Nothing good ever happens
late on a Friday night.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.387
Friday nights are for eating
cereal at 2:00 A.M.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.489
and watching reruns of that
cop show starring

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.557
the guy who sells
reverse mortgages.

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:15.328
You're not gonna fool me by
pretending to be a cop.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.363
I know you're here
to take my house.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.565
Also, it's incredibly
suspicious to have

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:22.034
a right-wing businessman
and mega-donor in charge

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.503
of a non-partisan agency
like the Postal Service.

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:27.339
You think of postal workers as
charming friends and neighbors

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:28.641
straight out of Mayberry.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.342
This is like if your town's
ice cream man

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:31.744
was replaced by Karl Rove.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.346
"Here you go, kid, one bullet
pop, that will be $6,000."

00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:35.682
They're made by Raytheon."

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.516
On top of that, DeJoy,
the former CEO

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:40.953
of a logistics company, also has
a massive conflict of interest.

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:43.055
According to his
financial disclosure,

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:46.325
he has anywhere from $30 million
to $75 million in assets

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.428
invested in competitors
to the post office,

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.695
which is absurd.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:51.864
That's like finding out
the new president of PETA

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.032
is the Colonel.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.800
"Your chickens will be safe
with me.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.170
Oh, these legs and thighs are
nice and juicy --

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.604
not for eating!"

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.707
Now, Trump and DeJoy say
the changes are necessary

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:03.276
because the post office
is losing money.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:06.145
In fact, you've probably heard
Trump complain about it

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.348
at one of his fake news
conferences.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:11.351
-They've lost so much money
over the decades.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:14.687
Nobody's ever -- nothing loses
money like the post office.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:17.557
It's been losing massive
amounts of money

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:20.026
over the last number
of decades.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:22.728
Massive amounts of money.
This is not something new.

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:25.998
This is something that's been
taking place for a long time.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:28.500
It loses a tremendous amount
of money.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.035
-Okay, first of all,
that's wrong.

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.704
The Postal Service turned
a profit as recently as 2006.

00:04:32.704 --> 00:04:34.540
Second, you're the last person
on Earth who should be

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.042
complaining about someone else
losing money.

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:39.479
You lost a billion,
one billion dollars,

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:41.580
in the '80s and '90s,
which was more than

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.116
any single taxpayer
in the country lost.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.519
And you also somehow managed
to lose money on casinos,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.187
which I didn't even think
was possible.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:49.889
I mean, casinos rake in cash.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.191
Last time I went to a casino,
I spent an hour playing a game

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.860
called The Money Eater.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.828
It was just a giant hole
you threw your chips into

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.131
and when you ran out,
it just screamed "Feed me!"

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:01.633
Also it makes no sense to say
the post office loses money.

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:03.169
It's a public service.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.704
You never hear people say the
fire department loses money.

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:08.975
We had start charging $50
per cat rescued from a tree.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:11.610
Of course, most owners I know,
most cat owners,

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.213
would also pay $50
if you left it in the tree.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:16.982
"She'll come down when she's
hungry, but I would love

00:05:16.982 --> 00:05:18.518
for her to learn a lesson.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.652
Now, Trump is not the only
Republican politician

00:05:20.652 --> 00:05:22.755
to complain that the post office
loses money.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.790
It's been a right-wing
talking point for years,

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.892
especially among those
who want to privatize

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.394
the postal service.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:31.030
The Trump administration
itself rolled out a plan

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.832
to do just that in 2018,

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:35.200
and right-wing billionaire
Charles Koch has been

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.904
campaigning to privatize
the postal service for decades,

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:41.607
which is shocking and craven
given that the postal service

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.276
is literally
in the Constitution.

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:46.979
In fact, it's as old as
the republic itself.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.281
So there was already
a years-long right-wing effort

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:51.417
to privatize one of America's
most cherished

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.419
public institutions,
the Postal Service.

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:56.588
Then came Trump, and he was
joined in his crusade

00:05:56.588 --> 00:05:59.224
by a bunch of soulless
right-wing husks

00:05:59.224 --> 00:06:01.660
who want to turn every
post office into one of those

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.695
combination
fast food restaurants.

00:06:03.695 --> 00:06:09.902
"Yeah, I'll take ten stamps and
a Doritos Locos Taco Supreme."

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:11.470
And look, it's absolutely true
that the post office

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.539
is struggling right now,
thanks in large part

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:16.709
to the pandemic and a decrease
in first-class mail volume,

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.644
even though package deliveries
have surged.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:21.413
But there's another reason the
post office loses money.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:24.049
And it's actually the fault of
the very same Republicans

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:27.019
who are now complaining that
the post office loses money.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:30.256
-In 2006, the Republican-led
Congress did pass a law

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:32.324
that affected the USPS's
bottom line.

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:35.160
It required the Postal Service
to prefund health benefits

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.995
for future retirees.

00:06:36.995 --> 00:06:39.465
We talked to experts who said
that because of this law,

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.667
USPS had to pay more
than $6 billion

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.335
that it really wasn't ready for.

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:47.173
So before the law, USPS paid out
these benefits as they came due.

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:50.709
And they point out that no other
agency has these restrictions.

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:52.445
So without the law,
the postal service

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:53.980
would definitely be
better off.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.983
-That's right.
In 2006, Republicans forced

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:59.584
the post office to pay
75 years

00:06:59.584 --> 00:07:02.722
of health fund benefits
in advance, which is insane.

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:06.058
Who knows what postal service
will even look like in 75 years?

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.593
Might just be a chip
in your brain

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.795
and you'll check the mail
by winking.

00:07:09.795 --> 00:07:12.264
"Oh, damn it, my student loan
officer found me."

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:16.869
I'm -- [ Laughing ]
I'm really bad at winking.

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:19.371
So without that law --
I can't get my mail anymore.

00:07:19.371 --> 00:07:21.574
So without that law, it's very
likely the post office

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:24.010
could have been operating at
a profit before the pandemic.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.646
In fact, from 2003 to 2006,

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:29.715
the Postal Service actually
did operate at a profit,

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:32.985
until the 2006 law
wrecked their finances.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.254
-From 2003 through 2006,

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:39.392
USPS recorded a total
$9.3 billion profit.

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:41.893
That all changed
at the end of 2006.

00:07:41.893 --> 00:07:44.463
Enter the Postal Accountability
and Enhancement Act,

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.932
which was passed by the
Republican-controlled Congress

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:49.401
and signed into law by
President George W. Bush.

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:51.437
It required the post office
to calculate

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.638
all of its retiree pension
and health care costs

00:07:53.638 --> 00:07:55.441
for the next 75 years,

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:58.077
including for people
it hadn't even hired yet,

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:01.413
and put away enough over the
next ten years to cover them.

00:08:01.413 --> 00:08:03.415
To put this in perspective,
that would be like

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:05.918
you only working from
age 18 to 28

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:07.486
and then expecting you
to live on that income

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:09.354
until you were 103
years old.

00:08:09.354 --> 00:08:11.924
-Yeah, exactly.
Imagine working for ten years

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:13.926
then living off that until
you're 103.

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:17.129
The only person who's ever
done it is Rudy Giuliani.

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:19.465
Without this law, the Postal
Service would have actually

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:22.167
recorded operating profits
in the last six years.

00:08:22.167 --> 00:08:24.737
Instead, it's now in
a dire financial situation

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:27.707
thanks to a requirement
that virtually no other

00:08:27.707 --> 00:08:30.409
government agency or company
has to deal with.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:33.345
-There is Congressional
legislation that required them

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:36.248
to prefund their pension
liabilities in a way

00:08:36.248 --> 00:08:37.750
that basically no one else
has to,

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.252
which has created an enormous
burden on their balance sheet.

00:08:40.252 --> 00:08:42.722
-They're definitely in trouble.
And what you mentioned,

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:44.490
the prefunding requirement,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:48.126
literally having to pay for --
or set aside money

00:08:48.126 --> 00:08:51.630
for the workers that haven't
even been born yet

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.233
that will be coming in
75 years down the road

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:57.870
is the primary reason
prior to the pandemic.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.371
-Just think about that.

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:01.573
They had to pay for retirement
benefits for workers

00:09:01.573 --> 00:09:03.308
who hadn't
even been born yet.

00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:05.344
That's like going out on
a first date and saying,

00:09:05.344 --> 00:09:07.012
"I had a great time tonight.
What do you say

00:09:07.012 --> 00:09:08.714
we go back to my place
and open up

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:11.283
a 529 college savings plan
for our eventual children?"

00:09:11.283 --> 00:09:12.718
It made no sense.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.353
And it weakened the postal
service dramatically.

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:17.322
Now the post office
desperately needs a bailout

00:09:17.322 --> 00:09:20.159
of as much as
$25 billion from Congress.

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:22.928
Which if you ask me,
we should immediately do.

00:09:22.928 --> 00:09:25.097
$25 billion is nothing compared

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:28.433
to the $740 billion
Pentagon budget.

00:09:28.433 --> 00:09:30.268
You're telling me you can't
find a billionaire to buy

00:09:30.268 --> 00:09:31.637
an f-15 or two?

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:33.672
Richard Branson definitely
has the vibe of a guy

00:09:33.672 --> 00:09:35.207
who wants to wind to blow
through his hair

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.809
at 1,800 miles an hour.

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:38.611
And yes, I say that joke
knowing my hair

00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:40.479
is getting more Bransony
by the day.

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.348
And yet, rather than spend
the money needed

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:44.684
to shore up of one his country's
most vital

00:09:44.684 --> 00:09:46.885
and cherished institutions,
Trump and the GOP

00:09:46.885 --> 00:09:49.821
are using the financial
situation as an opportunity

00:09:49.821 --> 00:09:52.625
to destroy the post office
for their own political gain.

00:09:52.625 --> 00:09:55.527
Just this weekend, "Politico"
reported that Trump's aides

00:09:55.527 --> 00:09:57.263
are exploring
executive actions

00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:58.997
to curb voting by mail,

00:09:58.997 --> 00:10:01.767
including everything from
directing the postal service

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:05.137
to not deliver certain ballots
to stopping local officials

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:06.905
from counting them
after Election Day.

00:10:06.905 --> 00:10:08.340
That is chilling.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.942
The President thinks
he can just decide

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:11.677
which votes count
and which ones don't.

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:14.012
Soon he's going to start
crossing out ballots himself

00:10:14.012 --> 00:10:17.316
and we'll all know because
he'll sign them himself.

00:10:17.316 --> 00:10:18.784
Whether or not Trump
actually succeeds

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:21.620
in stopping mail-in voting
is almost beside the point.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.455
Either way,
he's sowing confusion,

00:10:23.455 --> 00:10:25.157
setting up lengthy
court battles,

00:10:25.157 --> 00:10:27.593
and laying the groundwork to
claim the results are disputed,

00:10:27.593 --> 00:10:29.028
even if they're not.

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:30.963
He's made that as clear
as possible.

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:33.632
-I don't want to see
an election --

00:10:33.632 --> 00:10:37.169
you know, so many years
I've been watching elections --

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:39.605
and they say the projected
winner or the winner

00:10:39.605 --> 00:10:40.972
of the election.

00:10:40.972 --> 00:10:43.842
I don't want to see that
take place in a week

00:10:43.842 --> 00:10:46.178
after November 3rd,
or a month,

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:48.881
or frankly, with litigation

00:10:48.881 --> 00:10:51.349
and everything else
that can happen, years.

00:10:51.349 --> 00:10:55.153
Years. Or you never even
know who won the election.

00:10:55.153 --> 00:10:56.922
I want to have the result
of the election.

00:10:56.922 --> 00:11:00.592
I don't want to be waiting
around for weeks and months.

00:11:00.592 --> 00:11:04.029
And literally, potentially,
if you really did it right,

00:11:04.029 --> 00:11:05.831
years,
because you'll never know.

00:11:05.831 --> 00:11:07.532
I want to have the election.

00:11:07.532 --> 00:11:10.202
But I also don't want to have to
wait for three months

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:13.171
and then find out that
the ballots are all missing

00:11:13.171 --> 00:11:15.374
and the election
doesn't mean anything.

00:11:15.374 --> 00:11:16.775
That's what's going to happen.

00:11:16.775 --> 00:11:19.344
-It's only going to happen
if you make it happen.

00:11:19.344 --> 00:11:21.213
Trump's like a loan shark
telling you,

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:23.248
"I'd hate to see your
thumbs get broken."

00:11:23.248 --> 00:11:25.918
We can have a safe,
successful election

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:28.687
if we just adequately fund
and protect the post office.

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:30.522
You won't have to wait
years for results.

00:11:30.522 --> 00:11:32.157
But even if we did,
why are you complaining?

00:11:32.157 --> 00:11:34.493
Waiting around is like the
one thing you're good at.

00:11:34.493 --> 00:11:37.829
Your favorite sport is
98% waiting around.

00:11:37.829 --> 00:11:39.831
You spend most of your days
sitting in your bedroom

00:11:39.831 --> 00:11:41.901
watching TV and loitering
on the White House lawn

00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:44.003
like you're waiting
for a cross-town bus.

00:11:44.003 --> 00:11:46.038
You should be smoking
a cigarette, saying,

00:11:46.038 --> 00:11:48.941
"I should have taken --
I should have taken the M-66.

00:11:48.941 --> 00:11:51.610
Couldn't decide how to hold
my cigarette."

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:53.178
What do you think,
Trump like this,

00:11:53.178 --> 00:11:55.013
or Trump like this?"
Either way.

00:11:55.013 --> 00:11:57.349
Trump is openly trying to
disrupt timely delivery

00:11:57.349 --> 00:11:58.784
of the mail ahead of
a November election

00:11:58.784 --> 00:12:01.853
that will almost certainly
rely on an unprecedented surge

00:12:01.853 --> 00:12:03.622
in mail-in balloting

00:12:03.622 --> 00:12:05.924
because of the deadly plague
he failed to stop.

00:12:05.924 --> 00:12:08.827
DeJoy has already announced
major operational changes

00:12:08.827 --> 00:12:11.196
last month, including
slower mail delivery,

00:12:11.196 --> 00:12:13.465
post offices have been
slashing hours,

00:12:13.465 --> 00:12:15.867
local union leaders
and carriers say

00:12:15.867 --> 00:12:18.871
mail is piling up in offices
unscanned and unsorted.

00:12:18.871 --> 00:12:20.972
It's gotten so bad
a Democratic Senator

00:12:20.972 --> 00:12:24.510
is finally opening an
investigation into the delays.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.946
-We have folks who rely on the
Postal Service for our checks,

00:12:27.946 --> 00:12:30.616
Social Security checks,
paychecks,

00:12:30.616 --> 00:12:32.784
prescription medicines
that are coming in.

00:12:32.784 --> 00:12:34.552
I'm hearing from folks,
letter carriers

00:12:34.552 --> 00:12:36.622
and postal workers that
are saying they're seeing

00:12:36.622 --> 00:12:40.358
piles of mail they've never seen
before in their post offices.

00:12:40.358 --> 00:12:42.661
-That's insane.
Mail's not supposed to pile up

00:12:42.661 --> 00:12:44.629
in post offices,
it's supposed to pile up

00:12:44.629 --> 00:12:45.931
on your kitchen table.

00:12:45.931 --> 00:12:47.833
until one day
a mustachioed stranger

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:49.635
comes to take your house away.

00:12:49.635 --> 00:12:52.137
"Time to pay the piper,
old friend."

00:12:52.137 --> 00:12:54.339
"But you said you weren't going
to take my house."

00:12:54.339 --> 00:12:55.774
"I fibbed.

00:12:55.774 --> 00:12:59.478
I distracted you with my
mustache, and I fibbed."

00:12:59.478 --> 00:13:01.814
And letting mail pile up
is heresy

00:13:01.814 --> 00:13:03.682
for postal workers
who pride themselves

00:13:03.682 --> 00:13:05.350
on timely mail delivery.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:07.419
Remember their motto,
"Neither snow nor rain

00:13:07.419 --> 00:13:09.121
nor heat nor gloom of night"?

00:13:09.121 --> 00:13:11.290
That's why Trump would have been
a terrible mailman.

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:13.125
He would have seen one cloud
on the horizon

00:13:13.125 --> 00:13:14.860
and dumped his mailbag
in the East River

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.161
and headed for the OTB.

00:13:16.161 --> 00:13:18.597
"They'll never catch me.
Oh, no!

00:13:18.597 --> 00:13:21.133
Oh, no, since when does
paper float?"

00:13:21.133 --> 00:13:22.634
This is all Trump has left.

00:13:22.634 --> 00:13:25.471
He and the Republican Party have
given up on fairly winning

00:13:25.471 --> 00:13:27.372
a majority of votes,
so now they're trying

00:13:27.372 --> 00:13:28.974
to undermine
the election itself.

00:13:28.974 --> 00:13:31.977
Because Trump knows that if we
have a safe and fair election

00:13:31.977 --> 00:13:34.413
in which everyone
can easily participate,

00:13:34.413 --> 00:13:36.181
he has no chance of
being the --

00:13:36.181 --> 00:13:38.584
-Projected winner or the
winner of the election.

00:13:38.584 --> 00:13:40.752
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:13:40.752 --> 00:13:44.190
♪♪

00:13:46.558 --> 00:13:49.528
-So excited to hear
your feedback, Larry.

00:13:49.528 --> 00:13:51.096
